      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Spirits_of_Ellenton_(50327023837).jpg",
      "width": 4800,
      "height": 3600,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "Savannah River Site",
      "description": "On Nov. 28, 1950, the Atomic Energy Commission and the DuPont Company announced the Savannah River Plant would be built on 300 square miles of Aiken, Barnwell, and Allendale counties. This included the towns of Ellenton and Dunbarton. Many of the residents moved themselves, and in some cases, their homes to New Ellenton and neighboring communities. Eventually, most of what remained of Ellenton were the paved streets, curbs, driveways, and walkways. About 6,000 people and 6,000 graves were relocated during the move.\nBy: P.J. Perea, Savannah River Ecology Laboratory, University of Georgia",
